  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "This recipe serves 4 and is ready in about 30 minutes."
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Oyakodon is one of Japan's most-loved weeknight dinners. The name means 'parent and child bowl', referring to the chicken and egg cooked together. The key is catching the egg just before it fully sets."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "This is a"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "donburi"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "dish, so the rice matters. Use short-grain Japanese rice, cooked until fluffy and slightly sticky. Start the rice before you begin the sauce."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What you need"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "ingredientsList",
        "attrs": {
          "defaultServings": 4,
          "items": [
            {
